\f0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 I'll start by studying IRCAM's 
\f1\fs26 eolian harp.maxpat
\f0\fs24  and the manual pages it relies on. Then I'll build one 8-voice instrument here in my workspace and send it to you. I won't write anything into your Berlin folder unless you approve it.\
I have what I need from the manual and IRCAM's examples. Here's the plan before I build:\
The Lua logic checks out against a mock of the API. Now the two Max patches.\
I've built the 8 eolian harps as three files: a main patch, one voice abstraction it uses 8 times, and one shared Lua model. I haven't run them in Max yet, because Max can't run in my workspace, so the first launch on your Mac is the real test.\

\f2\b How a voice works
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-1342\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Strings:
\f0\b0  each voice is one 
\f1\fs26 modalys~
\f0\fs24  with 5 strings, built in 
\f1\fs26 mlys.lua
\f0\fs24  and read from 
\f1\fs26 eolian_voice.lua
\f0\fs24 . All 8 voices load that same file, so you edit the model in one place and press 
\f2\b rebuild all
\f0\b0 .\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Wind:
\f0\b0  IRCAM's harp is driven by a sound file. Here each voice instead gets its own noise with slow gusts, sent into the strings as a force. Motion in wedge k sets the wind strength for voice k. It also moves the noise band upward, so stronger wind brings out higher harmonics, as on a real aeolian harp. Wind rises in 10 ms and dies away over 0.5 s.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Output:
\f0\b0  the 8 voices go to 
\f1\fs26 mc.pack~ 8
\f0\fs24 , then 
\f1\fs26 mc.send~ hkw_harps 8
\f0\fs24 . In the Berlin project, add 
\f1\fs26 [mc.receive~ hkw_harps 8]
\f0\fs24  
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  
\f1\fs26 speaker_map
\f0\fs24 . There's also a quiet stereo mix for headphones.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-1342\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chords:
\f0\b0  each voice uses a 5-note pentatonic inside one church mode, keeping that mode's final and reciting tone. The authentic modes sit an octave above the plagal ones, so neighbouring wedges alternate high and low.\

