\cf0 The chords are editable message boxes in the main patch. Click one to apply it.\

\f2\b What F can drive.
\f0\b0  Pick one with the 1 / 2 / 3 buttons and listen:\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-1342\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Tonal centre:
\f0\b0  the whole voice bends \'b135 cents. F = 0.5 is in tune.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Brightness:
\f0\b0  the point where the wind touches the strings moves. Near the end of the string sounds brighter, near the middle sounds hollower.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Spread:
\f0\b0  the 5 strings detune away from each other by up to \'b120 cents, which makes them beat. F = 0 is in tune.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-1342\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The ranges, decay (loss) values and string positions are named constants at the top of the Lua file.\

